{#-
  The Home menu: a grid of picture (or icon) buttons on Home; on other menu
  views, one row per button with its name and a live status line. 'view' says how v2 builds the button's view:
    menu   a view of rows for 'entities' (areas), plus one subview each
    doors  views/doors.yaml ('entities': the door entries)
  'legacy' links to a view on the old dashboard (/ui-home/<legacy>) until it is
  ported.
  Status line: 'status' is an HA template (evaluated live). Without it, the
  row shows its 'sensors' (temperature/humidity) and the counts of its count
  groups (doors, locks, media, ...; a menu button: all its areas'), or 'idle'
  when there's nothing to show. 'image' may also be an HA template.
  'household' puts the status line in Home's Household window, hidden while
  it reads one of the listed (quiet) values; [] means always shown.
-#}
